WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.416
Draw two arcs around your operator.

00:00:04.696 --> 00:00:07.937
Everything they use often should sit inside the first one.

00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:14.062
When frequently used tools sit too far away, operators stretch hundreds of times a shift.

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:17.486
That means fatigue, strain and slower cycle times.

00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:22.324
It is one of the easiest problems to fix, yet one of the most common we see.

00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:29.202
The primary reach zone is within about 450 to 500 millimetres of the operator.

00:00:29.482 --> 00:00:34.685
Put the most-used items here: tape dispensers, cutters, scanners and hand tools.

00:00:34.965 --> 00:00:38.830
The secondary zone reaches up to about 1000 millimetres.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:42.520
Put less-used items here, like spare rolls and labels.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.202
Anything rarely used goes outside both.

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:47.230
Vertical space counts too:

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.611
shelves and pegboards just above the worktop keep items inside the primary zone.

00:00:53.211 --> 00:00:56.693
Furnisys accessories such as bin rails, pegboards,

00:00:56.693 --> 00:01:01.568
swing arms and shelves let you place items exactly inside these zones.

00:01:02.168 --> 00:01:04.192
Map the zones on one bench this week.

00:01:04.472 --> 00:01:05.982
What is sitting in the wrong place?

00:01:06.262 --> 00:01:09.887
Comment below, and next, apply 5S to the workstation.

00:01:10.487 --> 00:01:14.732
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

